# Option Pricing

A quantitative finance project exploring different methods for pricing financial options using Python, with plans to extend the implementation to C++.

## Project Goals

* Implement the Black–Scholes option pricing model
* Calculate option Greeks
* Explore Monte Carlo simulation for option pricing
* Implement a binomial pricing model
* Compare different numerical pricing methods
* Investigate implied volatility
* Explore the performance of Python and C++ implementations

## Methods

The project will cover:

* Black–Scholes model
* Monte Carlo simulation
* Binomial tree
* Numerical methods
* Risk measures and option Greeks

## Technologies

* Python
* NumPy
* SciPy
* Matplotlib
* C++ *(planned)*

## Status

🚧 Currently in development.
